    "show_share": true,
    "description": "\"Conditions relating to the heart are the leading cause of death in the world. In a developing country like Pakistan, both coronary artery disease and valvular heart diseases are prevalent,\" said Dr Hasanat Sharif, Consultant Cardiothoracic Surgeon at the Aga Khan University Hospital (AKUH). He was giving the presentation on \"Diagnosis and treatment of Heart Valve Disorder\" at 'Signs, Symptoms and Care' a monthly health awareness programme held on December 23, 2000.",
